amendment MEANING (LLR-300, LLR-301, LLR-322, TC-339, TC-340, TC-345, all blessed)\n?? docs/reviews/wi-834/023-ADJUDICATE-99601ff.md.requested","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":109,"oldLines":3,"newStart":109,"newLines":4,"lines":[" - 2026-10-09 — refresh under approval. Copied: low-level-requirements.toml (ref: WI-834); test-cases.toml (ref: WI-834). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."," - 2026-10-09 — refresh under approval. Copied: test-cases.toml (re-attested: TC-342, TC-343). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."," - 2026-10-09 — refresh under approval. Copied: low-level-requirements.toml (re-attested: LLR-047, LLR-320); test-cases.toml (re-attested: TC-342, TC-343). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes.","+- 2026-10-09 — refresh under approval. Copied: low-level-requirements.toml (re-attested: LLR-300, LLR-301, LLR-322); test-cases.toml (re-attested: TC-339, TC-340, TC-345). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":530,"oldLines":3,"newStart":530,"newLines":9,"lines":[" date = \"2026-10-09\""," approved = []"," reattested = [\"LLR-047\", \"LLR-320\", \"TC-342\", \"TC-343\"]","+","+[[act]]","+seq = 88","+date = \"2026-10-09\"","+approved = []","+reattested = [\"LLR-300\", \"LLR-301\", \"LLR-322\", \"TC-339\", \"TC-340\", \"TC-345\"]"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3172,"oldLines":8,"newStart":3172,"newLines":8,"lines":[" sr_refs = [\"SR-229\", \"SR-237\"]"," title = \"Coordinator context occupancy, lease, and drain latch\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_guard.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/shell_line.py\"","-code_symbol = \"GuardConfig/guard_config/Occupancy/read_occupancy/lease_dir/take/release/clear/hand_back/record_event/latch_reading/window_refusal/claim_refusal/on_blackout/launch_reason/model_clis/command_name/command_words/window_check/hooks_state/enable_hooks/on_monitored/on_session_start/on_pre_compact/classify_compaction/hook;claim;segments/Unreadable\"","-detail = \"guard_config reads the declared coordinator threshold and window: a non-positive, out-of-range or malformed threshold is off and a malformed window reads as the default. read_occupancy reads the newest valid assistant usage after the live transcript branch's latest compaction boundary, never a sidechain record, counting input and cached input; a record whose usage is malformed, partial or zero is skipped, and no valid usage reads as unknown, never zero. A primary-checkout lease names one coordinator session and its transcript. take refuses another holder; release frees the lease and clear unlatches it, each requiring and recording the owner's reason; hand_back accepts only the holder session and a handoff carrying a session prompt, frees the lease, and records the handoff; it refuses another or unnamed caller, whatever handoff it names, while naming the owner's release; it refuses the holder's own pending relaunch request, while a previous holder's request does not block it and is left for session_end's foreign-request refusal; with the guard off it returns before reading or writing. Elapsed time never transfers ownership. on_session_start installs a session as holder, unlatched, only when it presents the successor token the holder's exit wrote into the lease, and restates a latched drain to the holder's own resumed start. Only the holder's own hook payload on the holder's transcript is measured, never a subagent's. latch_reading latches drain when the unrounded reading reaches the threshold and retains it through lower readings, compaction and resume; it ends only through the owner's clear, the owner's release, the holder's hand-back, or a successor take. window_refusal runs before the dial on every claim route, including the dispatcher, naming the UTC end; the dispatcher remains exempt only from the context guard. claim_refusal identifies the claimant by the session id the agent CLI exports to its tool processes (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), refuses with no lease held or a claimant that is not the holder, and reads and latches the holder's transcript itself, so a refusal never depends on a hook having run; a claim holding the dispatch lock never calls it. While a window is armed hooks act at every dial and deny the closed list of the main session's Agent call, SendMessage call, Bash/PowerShell model-CLI command word, and a Bash/PowerShell line unreadable only because of an unclosed single quote, unclosed double quote, unclosed POSIX dollar quote, unclosed POSIX backtick substitution, unclosed dollar-parenthesis substitution, or unclosed PowerShell here-string. One quote-aware shell reading per dialect reads quoted assignments and env split strings as the shell does, treats quoted separators as data, reads substitutions in unquoted here-document and double-quoted PowerShell here-string bodies, and keeps quoted bodies as data; window_check exits nonzero inside it. At every SessionStart inside a window, hooks inject the blackout close-down instruction; each main session's monitored events inject it at that session's first monitored event in the window and every twentieth thereafter, counted per session per window: bring each open lane to its pause point, using a wrap-up adjudication for an active claim where needed; write the handoff naming each lane and its next obligation; request no relaunch; and end the session. Hook responses inject the latch instruction once and bounded reminders thereafter. PreCompact records trigger, occupancy and latch/request state; classify_compaction reports missed-threshold, manual and during-drain cases.\"","+code_symbol = \"GuardConfig/guard_config/Occupancy/read_occupancy/lease_dir/take/release/clear/hand_back/record_event/latch_reading/window_refusal/claim_refusal/on_blackout/launch_reason/model_clis/command_name/command_words/_assigned/window_check/hooks_state/enable_hooks/on_monitored/on_session_start/on_pre_compact/classify_compaction/hook;claim;segments/Unreadable/Word\"","+detail = \"guard_config reads the declared coordinator threshold and window: a non-positive, out-of-range or malformed threshold is off and a malformed window reads as the default. read_occupancy reads the newest valid assistant usage after the live transcript branch's latest compaction boundary, never a sidechain record, counting input and cached input; a record whose usage is malformed, partial or zero is skipped, and no valid usage reads as unknown, never zero. A primary-checkout lease names one coordinator session and its transcript. take refuses another holder; release frees the lease and clear unlatches it, each requiring and recording the owner's reason; hand_back accepts only the holder session and a handoff carrying a session prompt, frees the lease, and records the handoff; it refuses another or unnamed caller, whatever handoff it names, while naming the owner's release; it refuses the holder's own pending relaunch request, while a previous holder's request does not block it and is left for session_end's foreign-request refusal; with the guard off it returns before reading or writing. Elapsed time never transfers ownership. on_session_start installs a session as holder, unlatched, only when it presents the successor token the holder's exit wrote into the lease, and restates a latched drain to the holder's own resumed start. Only the holder's own hook payload on the holder's transcript is measured, never a subagent's. latch_reading latches drain when the unrounded reading reaches the threshold and retains it through lower readings, compaction and resume; it ends only through the owner's clear, the owner's release, the holder's hand-back, or a successor take. window_refusal runs before the dial on every claim route, including the dispatcher, naming the UTC end; the dispatcher remains exempt only from the context guard. claim_refusal identifies the claimant by the session id the agent CLI exports to its tool processes (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), refuses with no lease held or a claimant that is not the holder, and reads and latches the holder's transcript itself, so a refusal never depends on a hook having run; a claim holding the dispatch lock never calls it. While a window is armed hooks act at every dial and deny the closed list of the main session's Agent call, SendMessage call, Bash/PowerShell model-CLI command word, and a Bash/PowerShell line unreadable only because of an unclosed single quote, unclosed double quote, unclosed POSIX dollar quote, unclosed POSIX backtick substitution, unclosed dollar-parenthesis substitution, or unclosed PowerShell here-string. One quote-aware shell reading per dialect reads quoted assignments and env split strings as the shell does, reads a PowerShell assignment, recognised by an unquoted assignment operator wherever it stands (quotedness is known for every character of a word), whatever its target, as running its right-hand command; a quoted right-hand value and a variable right-hand value stay data, while a chained assignment whose final right-hand side is a command runs that command; treats quoted separators as data, reads substitutions in unquoted here-document and double-quoted PowerShell here-string bodies, and keeps quoted bodies as data; window_check exits nonzero inside it. At every SessionStart inside a window, hooks inject the blackout close-down instruction; each main session's monitored events inject it at that session's first monitored event in the window and every twentieth thereafter, counted per session per window: bring each open lane to its pause point, using a wrap-up adjudication for an active claim where needed; write the handoff naming each lane and its next obligation; request no relaunch; and end the session. Hook responses inject the latch instruction once and bounded reminders thereafter. PreCompact records trigger, occupancy and latch/request state; classify_compaction reports missed-threshold, manual and during-drain cases.\""," rationale = \"The context reading and lease are one admission fact: without one holder and a latched record, a tool-event observation can be missed and a later claim can start new work after the coordinator should be closing out.\""," test_refs = \"TC-315;TC-316;TC-317\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":3185,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3185,"newLines":7,"lines":[" title = \"Coordinator relaunch request and exit acquisition\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_guard.py;scripts/coordinator-relaunch.cmd;scripts/coordinator-relaunch.sh\""," code_symbol = \"session_prompt/request_relaunch/on_blackout/blackout_session_end/session_end/window_check/launch_command/launch_detached/exec_claude/main\"","-detail = \"session_prompt extracts the one fenced session prompt from a handoff, preserving headings inside that fence as prompt text. request_relaunch refuses inside a blackout window and otherwise accepts only the lease holder and an existing handoff, then writes a same-session request atomically. The hook's on_blackout SessionEnd dispatch calls blackout_session_end to cancel a pending request and record blackout inside a window; otherwise session_end acts only for a true exit by that holder in its declared repository, rejects a foreign request, and atomically renames one request to acquire it and holds the store lock from that acquisition until the launch is confirmed or the request restored, so restoration never waits on the lock. It writes a fresh successor token into the lease and the handoff prompt to a file, invokes the platform launcher detached in the declared root with that file and token, and on any failure before launch confirmation restores the request and removes the successor token and the prompt file. launch_command selects the Windows or POSIX launcher; launch_detached waits through its grace period and confirms only a still-running launcher or one that exits zero. Each launcher enters the declared root, exports the token as PT_COORDINATOR_TAKE for the successor's SessionStart take, and starts claude with the prompt as one argument: the POSIX one in a new terminal, the Windows one through exec_claude, which invokes claude with the extracted prompt. main dispatches the guard operations; reopening a session with the context latch still set needs the owner recorded clear.\"","+detail = \"session_prompt extracts the one fenced session prompt from a handoff, preserving headings inside that fence as prompt text. request_relaunch refuses inside a blackout window and otherwise accepts only the lease holder and an existing handoff, then writes a same-session request atomically. The hook's on_blackout SessionEnd dispatch calls blackout_session_end to cancel a pending request and record blackout inside a window; otherwise session_end acts only for a true exit by that holder in its declared repository, rejects a foreign request, and atomically renames one request to acquire it and holds the store lock from that acquisition until the launch is confirmed or the request restored, so restoration never waits on the lock. It writes a fresh successor token into the lease and the handoff prompt to a file, invokes the platform launcher detached in the declared root with that file and token, and on any failure before launch confirmation restores the request and removes the successor token and the prompt file. launch_command selects the Windows or POSIX launcher; launch_detached waits through its grace period and confirms only a still-running launcher or one that exits zero. Each launcher enters the declared root, resolves one interpreter by running its virtual-environment candidate followed by the candidates from its dev-setup's ordinary runtime search, and takes the first that reports Python 3.11 or later as its executable path; it exits nonzero with guidance when none resolves, runs window_check on that interpreter, exports the token as PT_COORDINATOR_TAKE for the successor's SessionStart take, and starts claude with the prompt as one argument: the POSIX one in a new terminal, the Windows one through exec_claude, which invokes claude with the extracted prompt. main dispatches the guard operations; reopening a session with the context latch still set needs the owner recorded clear.\""," rationale = \"The request must be owned, durable and consumed once, because a close-out that launches twice can create two coordinators and a failed launch must leave the handoff recoverable.\""," test_refs = \"TC-318\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":3424,"oldLines":9,"newStart":3424,"newLines":9,"lines":[" [design.LLR-322]"," sr_refs = [\"SR-032\"]"," title = \"Dev-setup consents to coordinator-hook opt-in\"","-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.sh;project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.ps1;project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_guard.py\"","-code_symbol = \"offer_hooks/OfferHooks;hooks_state/enable_hooks\"","-detail = \"When the shipped coordinator-hook example declares guard hooks and the current settings leave them off, an interactive consent may enable them by merging the guard hooks into the settings while preserving existing hooks and unrelated settings. A declined offer changes neither configuration nor credentials, and an example with no guard hooks creates no settings change.\"","+module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.sh;project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.ps1;project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_guard.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/guard_hooks.py\"","+code_symbol = \"offer_hooks/OfferHooks;hooks_state/enable_hooks;guard_groups/bind/command_shapes/merged\"","+detail = \"When the shipped coordinator-hook example declares guard hooks and the machine-local settings leave them off, an interactive consent may enable them by merging the guard hooks into the machine-local settings, each command bound to the floor-resolved interpreter that runs the opt-in, replacing only the guard's own commands. A command is the guard's only when it has the exact shape the shipped example defines: an interpreter, either the example's own word or a bound absolute path, followed by the guard script and hook subcommand; every other command, including one that merely names the guard file, is preserved along with its group's configuration and unrelated settings, and a group is dropped only when no command remains. The committed project settings are never written and a re-run is idempotent. A declined offer changes neither configuration nor credentials, and an example with no guard hooks creates no settings change.\""," rationale = \"Coordinator hooks change a contributor's interactive environment, so an explicit opt-in preserves existing configuration and leaves a declined setup reversible.\""," test_refs = \"TC-345\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3444,"oldLines":9,"newStart":3444,"newLines":9,"lines":[" [test.TC-339]"," verifies = [\"SR-229\", \"LLR-300\", \"IF-271\", \"IF-274\", \"IF-275\", \"SR-237\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Exercise claims and hooks during blackout with the context guard off. Exercise quote-aware shell reading, expandable and literal here bodies, and unreadable-line denial. Assert every SessionStart inside a window provides the close-down instruction and, for each main session, its first monitored event in that window and every twentieth thereafter provide it; assert that the route registry supplies model-CLI names.\"","+method = \"Exercise claims and hooks during blackout with the context guard off. Exercise quote-aware shell reading, PowerShell assignments of any target form (property, index, array-type, scoped, comma list, chained), with the operator spaced or written against a word that holds a quoted piece, and with command, quoted and variable right-hand sides, expandable and literal here bodies, and unreadable-line denial. Assert every SessionStart inside a window provides the close-down instruction and, for each main session, its first monitored event in that window and every twentieth thereafter provide it; assert that the route registry supplies model-CLI names.\""," tier = \"Smoke\"","-expected = \"Claims refuse on both routes and hooks deny only declared main-session launch forms. Quote-aware words and expandable bodies that launch a model are denied; quoted bodies are allowed; unreadable shell input is denied. The close-down instruction appears at every SessionStart inside a window and, for each main session, at its first monitored event in that window and every twentieth thereafter; it names each lane's handoff obligation, instructs no relaunch before the session ends, and model-CLI names follow the route registry.\"","+expected = \"Claims refuse on both routes and hooks deny only declared main-session launch forms. Quote-aware words, PowerShell assignments whose right-hand side runs a model, and expandable bodies that launch a model are denied; quoted bodies and quoted or variable right-hand values are allowed; unreadable shell input is denied. The close-down instruction appears at every SessionStart inside a window and, for each main session, at its first monitored event in that window and every twentieth thereafter; it names each lane's handoff obligation, instructs no relaunch before the session ends, and model-CLI names follow the route registry.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_claim_inside_the_window_is_refused_with_the_guard_off; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_dispatchers_claim_is_refused_inside_the_window; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hooks_deny_each_launch_form_with_the_guard_off; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hooks_allow_everything_else; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_subagents_call_is_never_denied; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_quoted_launch_form_is_denied; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_quoted_operator_is_not_a_command_boundary; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_an_unreadable_command_line_is_denied_inside_the_window; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_one_reading_keeps_quoted_text_in_its_word; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_json_array_template_names_its_cli; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_session_start_and_the_monitored_events_tell_the_close_down; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_cli_names_come_from_the_route_registry\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":3457,"oldLines":9,"newStart":3457,"newLines":9,"lines":[" level = \"Integration\""," method = \"Exercise relaunch requests and session-end handling during blackout.\""," tier = \"Smoke\"","-expected = \"No request is written during blackout and an existing request is cancelled at holder exit.\"","+expected = \"No request is written during blackout and an existing request is cancelled at holder exit; the guard command in injected instructions runs on the hook's own interpreter.\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_window_check_subcommand_exits_nonzero_inside; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_no_relaunch_is_written_inside_the_window; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_pending_relaunch_at_session_end_inside_the_window_is_cancelled\"","+evidence = \"tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_window_check_subcommand_exits_nonzero_inside; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_no_relaunch_is_written_inside_the_window; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_pending_relaunch_at_session_end_inside_the_window_is_cancelled; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_injected_guard_command_names_the_hooks_own_interpreter\""," status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "]},{"oldStart":3510,"oldLines":10,"newStart":3510,"newLines":10,"lines":[" [test.TC-345]"," verifies = [\"SR-032\", \"LLR-322\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Decline and accept the interactive coordinator-hook offer with existing settings, and run the hook command against examples with and without guard hooks.\"","+method = \"Decline and accept the interactive coordinator-hook offer with existing settings, and run the hook command against examples with and without guard hooks. Run an installed hook with a real Python below the floor first on PATH, where one is installed, and check the scaffold's git ignore list.\""," tier = \"Smoke\"","-expected = \"Consent enables the coordinator hooks by preserving existing settings and hooks; denial changes no configuration or credential; and an example without guard hooks changes nothing.\"","+expected = \"Consent enables the coordinator hooks in the machine-local settings, bound to the opt-in's interpreter, replacing only the guard's own commands defined by the shipped example's command shape, so a user command sharing a group with a guard command, including one that names the guard file, keeps its place and its group's matcher, and an older bare-python guard command is replaced by the bound one; a re-run changes nothing; an installed hook still denies with an older Python first on PATH; the machine-local file is git-ignored; denial changes no configuration or credential; and an example without guard hooks changes nothing.\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_denial_changes_no_configuration_or_credential; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_hooks_command_reports_and_switches_on; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hook_opt_in_merges_and_keeps_existing_hooks; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hook_opt_in_with_no_guard_hooks_changes_nothing\"","+evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_denial_changes_no_configuration_or_credential; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_hooks_command_reports_and_switches_on; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hook_opt_in_merges_and_keeps_existing_hooks; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hook_opt_in_with_no_guard_hooks_changes_nothing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_an_installed_hook_denies_with_an_older_python_first; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_scaffold_keeps_the_machine_local_settings_out_of_git\""," status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml"]}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfsX98xG1Vv4YdysgiB3d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six amended rows change meaning, and I blessed and re-attested each one. The verdict is `3f163849` and the re-attestation is `1403811a`. Both end with `WI: WI-834` and passed the commit hooks; the snapshot copied the LLR and TC registries without refusal.\n\n**amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=6`.**\n- **LLR-300 and TC-339:** the hook now treats a PowerShell assignment as running its right-hand command, whatever the target. Quoted or variable values stay data. This is the fix I ruled for in dispute 017.\n- **LLR-322 and TC-345:** the hook opt-in now writes only the machine-local `.claude/settings.local.json`, never the committed settings. Each hook command is bound to the interpreter that ran the opt-in, and only commands of the guard's exact shape are replaced, so the user's own commands survive.\n- **LLR-301 and TC-340:** the relaunch scripts now find a Python 3.11+ by actually running each candidate, exit with guidance if none qualifies, and run `window-check` on it. The guard command in injected instructions now names the hook's own interpreter.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- The code matches the new text: `coordinator_guard.py`, the new `kitlib/guard_hooks.py`, `kitlib/shell_line.py`, both relaunch scripts, the dev-setup templates and `gitignore.template`.\n- The affected suites gave `214 passed, 4 skipped`. The skips are three cases that need a terminal Windows lacks and one POSIX-only case.\n- The test that installs the hook and runs it with an older Python first on PATH really ran: this host has a Python below 3.11, and the hook still denied.\n- I probed 23 PowerShell forms against the hook and got no mismatch with LLR-300. The property, index, typed, scoped, comma-list, chained, `+=`, `??=` and no-space forms are denied. Quoted and variable values, a quoted `=` inside an index, comparisons and non-model commands are allowed.\n\nOne observation, not a return: LLR-301's new interpreter-resolution clause is tested, but the test is cited under TC-342 rather than LLR-301's own TC-318 or TC-340. A later spine pass could add it to TC-318's evidence.\n\nMy probe script is in the session scratchpad, not the repo. The `.requested` marker is left untracked for the coordinator."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":787,"cache_read_input_tokens":485667,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":787},"output_tokens":736,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d8d1fbc-6a42-4a02-9ec0-8f8d2b61c24c","uuid":"dd58824b-177f-49b3-93ec-c1bb29d80f45","timestamp":"2026-10-09T23:20:29.996Z","request_id":"req_011CfsX98eA4bT3rq7Fa8R7y"}
